# MPI Hostfile Configuration
# Format: hostname slots=N
# 
# Example for local testing:
localhost slots=4

# Example for cluster with multiple nodes:
# master-node slots=2
# worker-node-1 slots=4
# worker-node-2 slots=4
# worker-node-3 slots=2

# Notes:
# - 'slots' indicates how many MPI processes can run on that node
# - Set slots based on CPU cores available
# - Master node typically runs 1 process (rank 0)
# - Worker nodes run the remaining processes
# 
# For SSH-based clusters, ensure:
# 1. Passwordless SSH is configured between all nodes
# 2. The program binary and input files are accessible on all nodes
# 3. All nodes have the same MPI installation
